# Secrets
.env

# Client material
# The milestone brief is the client's document, not ours. It is deliberately kept out of the public
# repository and was purged from git history (2026-09-27) before the first push. It stays on the
# working copy for reference only. Do not re-add.
Docs/ProblemStatement.txt

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Virtualenv
.venv/

# Generated at build time
# NOTE: data/raw/ and data/processed/ are intentionally COMMITTED. The snapshot is the source
# of truth for reproducibility and offline operation (architecture.md §7.3, §18.1). The vector
# store and the model cache are large and rebuildable, so they are not.
data/chroma/
data/models/
data/chunks.jsonl
# Human-readable chunk + vector dump for inspection; regenerate from the store at any time.
data/chunks_and_vectors.txt
# Run record: carries a timestamp and a duration, so committing it would dirty the tree on every
# build. Reproducibility is anchored on data/raw/ and data/processed/ (committed) plus the
# config_hash and corpus_hash this file records.
data/build_report.json

# Phase 0 spike scratch: 3.3 MB of throwaway HTML/text for candidate URLs, most of them rejected.
# docs/corpus_matrix.md records the findings; Phase 3 re-fetches the 5 accepted sources into
# data/raw/ deterministically, so committing these would only duplicate the corpus.
data/raw/spike/
